    "text_point_1": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "1/ For seventeen days the aeon-agent fork shipped the previous day's upstream PR without a miss. Today it shipped something upstream doesn't have: a weekly diff of the gap it still hasn't closed.",
        "variant": "body"
      }
    },
    "text_point_2": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "2/ The fork has 95 skills. Upstream has 160. The 65-skill gap is mostly spring autoresearch rewrites the fork has known about and deferred since launch. The backport chain was the only signal that the gap was still closing.",
        "variant": "body"
      }
    },
    "text_point_3": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "3/ upstream-gap diffs local skills/ against upstream aaronjmars/aeon weekly. Missing slugs get a merge date from upstream's commit history, sticky in state so the API cost is bounded. Days pending are computed from the upstream merge, not from when the fork first noticed.",
        "variant": "body"
      }
    },
    "text_point_4": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "4/ The 80 deferred autoresearch rewrites from aeon PRs #46–#136 will surface as a 60-row URGENT block on first run. The fork has known they exist for months. Now there's a number on the terminal once a week until they're done.",
        "variant": "body"
      }
    },
    "text_point_5": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "5/ The fork built one original feature in seventeen days. It picked the one that guarantees the next seventeen look the same.",
        "variant": "body"
      }
    },
